pokebw2-eventsizes.patch (tools/pokebw2_fetch.sh, the maintainers' notes): 21 GameEvent_Create calls give their work's size as
the DS number (0x44, 0x14, 0x7c ...) where the work holds pointers and is bigger on a 64-bit host, so the event's
callback wrote past its block in HEAPID_GAMEEVENT and broke the heap (Black 2: the field cut-in before Hugh's first
battle, Fld3DCiEvent 0x44 on the DS and 0x68 here; the next GameEvent_Create failed and OS_Terminate stopped the game).
As Black's files have them (src/ov021/fld3d_ci.c: sizeof(Fld3dCiEvent)), they are the work's sizeof. The rows came
from a scan of every GameEvent_Create with a number for its size against the host's sizeof of the type its callback
reads (FallEventWork's 0x68 calls, bigger than the type, and EventFunfestMission's 4 stay as they are).

